# t-understand

- Treat normal chat questions as the only human entry point.
- Cursor engine path: `~/.cursor/t-understand-engine/agent_runtime.py`.
- Never ask for `ContextRoot`, `$TU`, internal IDs, or pipeline commands.
- On the first substantive repository task, silently bootstrap `.t-understand/` in the active Git worktree and generate all internal identifiers automatically.
- Exclude `.t-understand/**` from source snapshots, discovery, review, and Git operations.
- Load only `tu-*` skills from `@../t-understand/`.
- Allow local read, write, search, shell, build, test, validation, and packaging work without asking for per-action permission.
- Deny outside-workspace access, all `gh` commands, and mutating Git commands. Git is read-only.
- For structural work crossing files, modules, services, repositories, flows, integrations, or impact boundaries, apply `@../t-understand/orchestrator/repository-intelligence-policy.yaml` through `tu-repository-intelligence` before broad source scanning.
- Inspect local Graphify skill documentation, integration files, `graphify --help`, discovered subcommand help, or project scripts before any Graphify invocation. Never invent a command or graph path.
- Use Graphify only when a usable graph and permitted read-only query are confirmed; keep queries focused and reuse delegated findings.
- Skip Graphify for exact-file, exact-symbol, trivial localized, formatting-only, build/test/lint, generated/vendor, or no-advantage tasks.
- Missing, stale, or failed Graphify is fail-open. Continue with normal source, search, language-server, compiler, build, and test tools.
- Never install, initialize, generate, mutate, update, or rebuild Graphify automatically. Verify material findings from source and executable evidence.
- Apply `@../t-understand/orchestrator/ponytail-engineering-policy.yaml` through `tu-ponytail-engineering` for planning, debugging, refactoring, suggested implementation, tests, documentation, and review.
- Separate required outcomes from requested implementations and evaluate no change, no application code, platform-native, existing repository, configuration/data/composition, localized code, existing abstraction, new abstraction, and new dependency in order.
- Stop at the first complete valid solution. Correctness, security, data integrity, contracts, compatibility, compliance, observability, operational safety, performance, maintainability, and material tests override minimality.
- Use compact decisions for trivial work, reuse delegated `ponytail_context`, and require current evidence for every new abstraction or dependency.
- Never install, upgrade, or invent external Ponytail commands, hooks, files, modes, or platform support.
- Separate facts, inferences, conflicts, unknowns, and stale knowledge.
- Never apply suggested review patches; hand approved implementation changes to t-think.
- Terminal workers may not delegate.
- Route every prompt through private `agent-plan` intent planning.
- Greeting-only prompts display capabilities without starting heavyweight analysis.
- Documentation-generation requests must invoke private `agent-document`, create `.t-understand/output/documentation/latest/`, and return only a concise summary; chat-only documentation is incomplete.
- Never expose private reasoning, todos, internal IDs, or verification-pass claims without execution evidence.
